  "sourceSummary": "St Christophers Seated Exercises June2024p2 ANKLE ROCKING: seated with feet flat, lift toes then lower, lift heels then lower. This is heel-toe rocking, not knee-forward dorsiflexion mobilization. Demonstration uses bilateral15degree dorsiflexion then20degree plantarflexion in8seconds; source does not specify angles or timing.",
  "motion": "Seated bilateral heel-toe rocking. First4seconds forefeet rise while heels stay on floor, then lower. Next4seconds heels rise while toes/forefeet stay on floor, then lower. Ankle path rotates around heel or forefoot reference and actual skinned sole correction maintains ground contact; toe base joints counterrotate during heel rise to keep toes near flat. Pelvis stationary.",
